**ABOUT

This python program, ran in a command line interface, offers five choices to the user with the goal of giving them 
a more clear view of their finances. 

**HOW TO USE

The user will be prompted to enter a number and hit enter to choose their desired function.
NOTE: Only the exact numbers can be entered, either a 1, 2, 3, 4, or 5. The program currently has no input validation. 
The user will then respond to the prompts, using whole numbers or decimal numbers, but no special symbols (including $) except '.'
The program will then generate the desired output based on the choice. 

Choice 1: 
The first choice calculates yearly income by prompting the user to enter a "1" to calculate based off of hourly wage 
or a "2" to calculate based off of weekly income. If the user enters "1", it will prompt them for their hourly wage and 
average hours worked each week. If the user enters "2", it will ask for their weekly income. 
(Note all values can be entered as a whole number or decimal, but do not use any symbols other than '.') 
The program will then print their estimated yearly income. 

Choice 2: 
The second choice calculates yearly expenses by prompting the user to enter their estimated monthly expense at each 
expense category. These values can be entered as whole numbers or decimal numbers, and the program will print their estimated 
yearly expenses. 

Choice 3: 
The third choice calculates how long in weeks it will take to make a certain quantity of money by prompting the user to enter 
a "1" to calculate based off of hourly wage or a "2" to calculate based off of weekly income. If the user enters "1", it will 
prompt them for their hourly wage and average hours worked each week. If the user enters "2", it will ask for their weekly income. 
(Note all values can be entered as a whole number or decimal, but do not use any symbols other than '.') 
The program will then print how long in weeks it will take to make the desired quanitity of money.

Choice 4: 
The fourth choice creates a table depicting income and expenses by prompting the user for the name of the file it will create containing
HTML code that will create a table showing their income and expenses based on their answers to the prompts when ran in an HTML editor. 
The file will be made in the same directory that the program is located in. To view the table, copy and paste all the contents of the file 
into a HTML editor and run it. 
(link to a free HTML editor-> https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_editor.asp) 

Choice 5: 
The fifth choice ends the program. 

**INSTALL
To run the program, the user will need to put the source code file into a python compiler and run it. 
The below webiste contains instructions on how one may do this:
https://www.fabriziomusacchio.com/blog/2022-10-31-GitHub/

Note that the program's results are only as accurate as your estimations.
Enjoy!
